<div style="background-color: #1a5276; color: white; padding: 15px; text-align: center; border-radius: 8px; margin-bottom: 20px;">
    <h1 style="margin: 0;">Lesson Planner – Theme # A Mola Has Many Colors! – Lesson # 4</h1>
    <p style="margin: 5px 0 0 0; font-size: 1.1em;">Complete this planner five times per theme, once per lesson (Lesson 1 through Lesson 5).</p>
</div>

<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <tr>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 25%;"><b>Lesson #:</b> 4</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 75%;"><b>Skills Focus:</b> Writing</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Grade:</b> 4th Grade (CEFR: A1.2)</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Scenario:</b> The Beautiful Mola</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Theme:</b> A Mola Has Many Colors!</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Date(s):</b> From ___ to ___</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="2"><b>Learning Sequence Time:</b> 45–50 min</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="3">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Specific Objective:</b> Writing: productive: Compose simple personal letters or emails. interactive: Respond in writing to written questions from peers.</p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Learning Outcome:</b> Writing: Can compose simple personal letters about mola art (e.g., 'Dear Juan Carlos, I like the colorful molas.'). Can respond to peers' written questions about molas (e.g., 'What colors were used?' 'The mola is red and blue.'). Can revise letters or responses for clarity and correctness (e.g., add 'colorful' to describe the mola).</p>
        </td>
    </tr>
</table>

<h2 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 30px;">The Six Action-Oriented Approach (AOA) Lesson Stages</h2>
<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <thead>
        <tr>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; background-color: #f2f2f2; width: 33%;">Stage & Description</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; background-color: #f2f2f2; width: 33%;">Activities & Teacher Actions</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; background-color: #f2f2f2; width: 33%;">Estimated Date and Time</th>
        </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 8px;">STAGE 1 — Warm-up / Pre-task</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Engagement, Modeling and Clarification</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Warm-up:</b> The teacher displays various pictures of molas with different animals and colors. Students orally identify colors and shapes they see. Then, the teacher asks, "What do you like about this mola?" Students write one or two words on mini-whiteboards or scrap paper (e.g., 'colors,' 'turtle,' 'vibrant'). The teacher collects responses and highlights common words.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Modeling:</b> The teacher writes a simple sentence on the board: "A mola has many colors." Then, the teacher adds: "I like this mola because it is colorful." The teacher points to 'because' and explains it gives a reason. The teacher models writing the sentence clearly and slowly, emphasizing words like 'mola' /m/ and 'colors' /k/ and checking for spelling of simple words like 'red,' 'blue,' 'vibrant.'</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Clarification (CCQs):</b></p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; margin-left: 20px; padding: 0;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What does 'because' tell us?" (A reason.)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"If I write 'I like the mola...', what comes next?" (Because...)</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">[Date] <br> [Time: 8-10 min]</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 8px;">STAGE 2 — Presentation</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Input of new language/content connected to Scenario: "The Beautiful Mola".</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Material:</b> A simple, short personal letter (genre: letter, register: informal, format: handwritten text) from a child describing a mola. The letter will be displayed on a projector or as a handout.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Example Letter:</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">"Dear Juan Carlos,</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">I like the colorful molas. My favorite mola has a beautiful turtle. It is red and blue and yellow. I like this mola because it is vibrant and unique. The artists choose many colors carefully.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">From, Ana"</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Competence:</b> Written Expression (Composing simple sentences and short paragraphs to express preferences and descriptions about mola art).</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Comprehension tasks (for writing analysis):</b></p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; margin-left: 20px; padding: 0;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Students read the letter silently.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Teacher asks: "Who wrote this letter?" (Ana) "Who is it for?" (Juan Carlos)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What animal is on Ana's favorite mola?" (Turtle)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What colors does the mola have?" (Red, blue, yellow)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Why does Ana like this mola?" (Because it is vibrant and unique.) The teacher points to the sentence structure for reasons.</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">[Date] <br> [Time: 7-9 min]</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 8px;">STAGE 3 — Preparation / Practice</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Accuracy focus on Writing.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Skill & Content:</b> Writing sentences using 'because' for reasons, Present Simple for descriptions ('A mola has...'), and target vocabulary (mola, colors, vibrant, unique, turtle, butterfly, jaguar, turquoise, golden, round, carefully).</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Detailed Procedure:</b></p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: decimal; margin-left: 20px; padding: 0;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Sentence Completion (Controlled Practice):</b> Students receive a worksheet with sentences about molas to complete. They choose from a word bank including vocabulary like 'vibrant,' 'unique,' 'turtle,' 'butterfly,' 'jaguar,' 'because,' 'red,' 'blue.'
                        <br>Example: "This mola has a __________. It is __________ and __________. I like it __________ it is __________." (Expected: This mola has a *butterfly*. It is *red* and *golden*. I like it *because* it is *vibrant*.)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Guided Mola Description (Semi-Controlled Practice):</b> Students choose a mola picture from a selection provided by the teacher. Using sentence frames, they write three to four sentences describing it and expressing their preference.
                        <br>Sentence frames: "This mola has a __________. It has __________ and __________ colors. I like this mola because it is __________." They are encouraged to use adjectives like 'turquoise,' 'round,' 'traditional,' and adverbs like 'carefully.'</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Peer Sentence Check (Pair Interaction/Peer Check):</b> In pairs, students exchange their written mola descriptions. They read their partner's sentences and mark with a check if the sentences are clear and use correct words. They can also write a very simple written comment like "Good colors!" or "Nice mola!" This encourages acknowledging peers' contributions and provides initial written feedback, focusing on sociolinguistic competence.</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">[Date] <br> [Time: 15-17 min]</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 8px;">STAGE 4 — Performance / Production</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Communicative task where students USE the language in a realistic scenario: "The Beautiful Mola".</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Task Format:</b> Collaborative Written Exchange: Students will first compose a simple personal letter about a mola, and then respond in writing to a peer's written question about their mola.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Procedure:</b></p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: decimal; margin-left: 20px; padding: 0;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Part 1: Write a Letter:</b> Each student chooses a mola image (from a collection or one they drew in a previous lesson). They compose a simple letter (4-5 sentences) to a classmate following the model from Stage 2. They must describe their chosen mola, its colors (e.g., 'red,' 'orange,' 'vibrant'), and express why they like it using 'because' (e.g., 'I like this mola because it has a butterfly.'). They should include 2-3 vocabulary words (e.g., 'vibrant,' 'unique,' 'turtle,' 'creativity').</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Part 2: Exchange and Question:</b> Students exchange their letters with a partner. After reading their partner's letter, each student writes one question on their partner's letter about the mola (e.g., "What colors were used?" "Is it a unique design?" "Why do you like the jaguar mola?"). This is done in writing.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Part 3: Respond to Question:</b> Students receive their original letter back with a peer's question. They write a simple, short answer below the question. (e.g., "The mola is red and blue." or "Yes, it is very unique."). They revise their letters or responses for clarity and correctness (e.g., adding an adjective like 'colorful' if it helps).</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Focus:</b> Fluency in composing simple written messages, using 'because,' present simple, and relevant vocabulary to describe mola art and respond to direct questions. Emphasizes interactive writing.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">[Date] <br> [Time: 10-12 min]</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 8px;">STAGE 5 — Assessment / Post-task</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Formative assessment strategy.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Formative Assessment Strategy:</b> Teacher observation checklist during the writing activity, focusing on task completion and basic use of target language. Peer assessment checklist for basic correctness and clarity.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Assessment Task:</b> Students submit their personal letters with the peer's question and their written response.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Evaluation Criteria (Teacher Checklist):</b></p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: circle; margin-left: 20px; padding: 0;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Composes a simple personal letter about mola art (e.g., 'Dear Juan Carlos, I like the colorful molas.').</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Responds in writing to a peer's written question about a mola (e.g., 'The mola is red and blue.').</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Uses the conjunction 'because' to express a reason.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Uses at least 2 target vocabulary words (e.g., 'vibrant,' 'unique,' 'turtle').</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Shows clarity and basic correctness in writing (sentence structure, legible spelling).</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student Self-Assessment / Exit Ticket:</b> Students answer the following questions on an exit slip:</p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; margin-left: 20px; padding: 0;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"I can write a letter describing a mola: Yes / No"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"I can write why I like a mola using 'because': Yes / No"</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">[Date] <br> [Time: 5-7 min]</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 8px;">STAGE 6 — Reflection</h3>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student self-reflection prompt:</b></p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; margin-left: 20px; padding: 0;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What was easy or difficult for me when writing my letter or my answer today?"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What new words or sentences did I use to talk about molas?"</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Teacher reflection:</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Today, students successfully composed simple letters and responded to peers' questions. The use of sentence frames and a clear model letter was effective for guiding their writing at A1.2 level. Students showed good understanding of 'because' to express reasons. Some students needed more prompting to include specific adjectives like 'vibrant' or 'unique.' For next time, I need to ensure there are sufficient opportunities for students to revise their writing, perhaps with a short checklist for self-correction.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Connection to next lesson:</b> This writing practice will prepare students for Lesson 5, where they will integrate all four skills (Listening, Reading, Speaking, and Writing) to summarize information about molas and collaborate on a final creative project, possibly writing simple instructional steps ('First, cut the fabric...') for their mola project.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">[Date] <br> [Time: 5-7 min]</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>